{"parentUuid":"8810c7bc-fc1c-43cf-b605-b7ada1b4aa91","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/devin/repos/a2-ai/test-build-processes","sessionId":"7f22a452-0af5-4c0c-be1c-699e971cf878","version":"2.0.22","gitBranch":"main","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929","id":"msg_01JFhZKmuhM7yABVmyjLTCWa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I've successfully created a separate release pipeline for generating .deb packages. Here's what was created:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've set up a **separate deb-based release pipeline** that complements your existing simple binary release process. Here's what was created:\n\n### New Files Created:\n\n1. **`.goreleaser.yml`** - GoReleaser configuration that:\n   - Builds Rust binaries for x86_64 and aarch64\n   - Creates .deb packages with proper metadata\n   - Generates tar.gz archives\n   - Includes checksums\n\n2. **`scripts/postinstall.sh`** - Post-installation hook that:\n   - Makes the binary executable\n   - Displays installation messages\n   - Can be extended with additional setup (commented examples included)\n\n3. **`scripts/preremove.sh`** - Pre-removal hook that:\n   - Cleans up before package removal\n   - Can be extended with cleanup tasks (commented examples included)\n\n4. **`.github/workflows/release-deb.yml`** - Multi-stage workflow that:\n   - **Stage 1 (Build-Binaries)**: Builds binaries on AlmaLinux 8 containers for both x86_64 and aarch64\n   - **Stage 2 (Package-Deb)**: Uses GoReleaser on native runners to create .deb packages\n   - **Stage 3 (Create-Release)**: Assembles all artifacts and creates a GitHub release\n\n5. **`RELEASE.md`** - Documentation explaining:\n   - Both release pipelines\n   - How to trigger each one\n   - Comparison between the two approaches\n   - Use cases for each\n\n### Key Differences from Existing Pipeline:\n\n| Feature | Existing (`v*.*.*`) | New Deb Pipeline (`deb-v*.*.*`) |\n|---------|---------------------|-----------------------------------|\n| **Trigger** | `v0.1.0` | `deb-v0.1.0` |\n| **Stages** | 2 (Build + Release) | 3 (Build + Package + Release) |\n| **Output** | tar.gz only | .deb + tar.gz + checksums |\n| **Hooks** | None | postinstall.sh, preremove.sh |\n| **Tool** | Native cargo | cargo + GoReleaser |\n\n### How to Use:\n\n**Trigger the new deb release pipeline:**\n```bash\ngit tag deb-v0.1.0\ngit push origin deb-v0.1.0\n```\n\n**Install the resulting .deb:**\n```bash\nsudo dpkg -i test-build-processes_0.1.0_amd64.deb\n```\n\nThe multi-stage approach ensures binaries are built on AlmaLinux 8 (for glibc 2.28 compatibility) while GoReleaser runs on native Ubuntu runners to assemble the .deb packages with proper hooks and metadata."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":264,"cache_read_input_tokens":27757,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":264,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":691,"service_tier":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CUEpGhXh4yrmWWk5mmdgz","type":"assistant","uuid":"07e4c274-3fea-4ece-8590-48ad3217aa9e","timestamp":"2025-10-18T14:24:10.881Z"}
